1
00:00:02,302 --> 00:00:05,760
Robin Hood!

2
00:00:05,872 --> 00:00:07,305
This way!

3
00:00:07,374 --> 00:00:10,901
- Come on!
- Come on!

4
00:00:16,816 --> 00:00:20,274
Robin, the Sheriff's in range.
It's the perfect shot.

5
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:23,117
One arrow. It's the end
of his reign of terror.

6
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:26,886
For your crimes against the people
of Nottingham, Sheriff.

7
00:00:28,128 --> 00:00:30,392
You're rubbish, Daniel.
It's my turn with the bow.

8
00:00:30,497 --> 00:00:32,624
- I'm Robin.
- You're always Robin.

9
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:34,599
I get this boring piece of tree.

10
00:00:36,436 --> 00:00:37,903
Hey.

11
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:45,378
Mark, get up.

12
00:01:15,542 --> 00:01:17,100
Now.

13
00:01:21,214 --> 00:01:22,738
Whoa.

14
00:01:22,816 --> 00:01:26,718
You see? I told you I could do it.
Nothing can penetrate it.

15
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:30,885
- Excellent work.
- What else did you expect?

16
00:01:30,957 --> 00:01:34,950
Unfortunately, this secret
cannot leave the forest.

17
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:39,694
Oh!

18
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:42,125
Get them!

19
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:38,256
Go round. Go round!

20
00:02:38,324 --> 00:02:40,087
Mark, come on.

21
00:03:23,536 --> 00:03:25,470
Come on out.

22
00:03:27,106 --> 00:03:30,234
You can trust me. I'm lord of Locksley.

23
00:03:52,799 --> 00:03:54,357
Shh.

24
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:58,370
Lord of Locksley.

25
00:03:58,438 --> 00:04:00,633
- Why...
- It's all right.

26
00:04:00,707 --> 00:04:04,074
Hang on, I know you. You were Marian's
table boy at Knighton Hall.

27
00:04:04,143 --> 00:04:06,941
How do you know that?

28
00:04:07,547 --> 00:04:12,143
What happened? I know Gisborne's
up to something cos I've been tracking him.

29
00:04:12,218 --> 00:04:14,482
- I don't trust you.
- All right.

30
00:04:15,154 --> 00:04:16,781
Tell me your name.

31
00:04:16,856 --> 00:04:18,721
- Daniel.
- Daniel.

32
00:04:18,791 --> 00:04:21,817
- Do you know who I am?
- No.

33
00:04:21,894 --> 00:04:23,361
I'm Robin Hood.

34
00:04:35,808 --> 00:04:37,901
So what were you doing up there?

35
00:04:37,977 --> 00:04:39,740
Nothing. Playing.

36
00:04:41,547 --> 00:04:44,482
- At Robin Hood.
- What, playing a loser?

37
00:04:44,550 --> 00:04:46,313
We didn't see anything, sir.

38
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:53,687
If you didn't see anything, why would
you say you didn't see anything?

39
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,728
We won't say anything, sir.

40
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:59,098
You can be sure of that.

41
00:05:02,402 --> 00:05:04,165
Wait.

42
00:05:05,371 --> 00:05:07,862
We can use them. Send them to the mine.

43
00:05:08,941 --> 00:05:12,308
And send word to the Sheriff - "success".

44
00:05:12,378 --> 00:05:14,141
Finally.

45
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:20,751
Gisborne's got my friends.
He's got my friends.

46
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:24,483
I can help you with your friends
but I need you to tell me what you saw.

47
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:27,252
A man,

48
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,522
they shot him but he didn't die.

49
00:05:29,595 --> 00:05:33,463
The arrows bounced off
and then Sir Guy killed him with a knife.

50
00:05:33,533 --> 00:05:37,560
- And now he's gonna kill my friends.
- Whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa.

51
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:41,069
- The arrows bounced off what?
- Armor.

52
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:43,267
He was wearing armor, funny armor.

53
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:47,479
Let's see about your friends,
shall we? Come on.

54
00:05:49,048 --> 00:05:51,539
- Here.
- I thought you said chicken.

55
00:05:51,617 --> 00:05:54,848
- Well...
- That's a small chicken, Much.

56
00:05:54,921 --> 00:05:57,515
Yeah, again.

57
00:05:57,590 --> 00:06:00,957
And have you seen in the trees?
No squirrels lately.

58
00:06:02,829 --> 00:06:07,163
- It's not squirrel.
- And what happened to the vegetables, huh?

59
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,992
All you eat is bread and meat?

60
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:14,699
We're surrounded by
edible berries and leaves.

61
00:06:14,774 --> 00:06:16,969
Where's the fruit, the salad?

62
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:19,876
- Salad?
- Men eating leaves?

63
00:06:19,946 --> 00:06:21,811
There's only one use for leaves around here

64
00:06:21,914 --> 00:06:24,678
and you wouldn't want
to be eating them afterwards.

65
00:06:24,751 --> 00:06:27,982
Up. We need to go.

66
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:32,115
This is Daniel. His friends are in danger
and, if I'm not much mistaken, so are we.

67
00:06:32,191 --> 00:06:35,592
- What's up?
- It's Gisborne. He's creating a new armor.

68
00:06:36,329 --> 00:06:38,957
We need to take his toys away
so arm yourselves.

69
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:43,763
Little John. Will.

70
00:06:43,836 --> 00:06:45,701
Allan A Dale.

71
00:06:45,772 --> 00:06:47,797
And you must be Djaq, the Saracen.

72
00:06:47,874 --> 00:06:49,865
Wow.

73
00:06:49,942 --> 00:06:52,206
Sorry, who are you?

74
00:06:52,278 --> 00:06:55,338
That, that's Much.

75
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:57,975
Oh, yes, the servant.

76
00:07:02,054 --> 00:07:03,988
Very funny.

77
00:07:11,197 --> 00:07:13,529
- What?
- Nothing.

78
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,726
It's just I thought you'd be...

79
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:18,297
taller.

80
00:07:18,371 --> 00:07:22,239
- I'm quite tall.
- But you know, like a giant.

81
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,940
Men tend to lie about their size.

82
00:07:25,845 --> 00:07:28,075
You ready? Give me that.

83
00:07:29,415 --> 00:07:31,906
You won't be needing it. Come on, let's go.

84
00:07:39,926 --> 00:07:41,894
They've gone.

85
00:07:55,942 --> 00:07:58,877
It's Mark's. See, the M?

86
00:08:01,447 --> 00:08:03,142
That's good.

87
00:08:03,216 --> 00:08:05,480
We play outlaws.

88
00:08:05,551 --> 00:08:07,416
I'm Robin Hood.

89
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:09,978
I hope you're better
at playing Robin that I am.

90
00:08:10,056 --> 00:08:12,217
No.

91
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:14,225
I let go of his hand.

92
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:16,625
Gisborne's lot were coming and I just ran.

93
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:19,561
- Well then, you did the right thing.
- Really?

94
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:24,294
If you hadn't run, you would've been caught,
too, and what good is that?

95
00:08:25,538 --> 00:08:29,269
Listen, sometimes, in the heat of battle...

96
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:32,871
there isn't time to watch your gang's back.

97
00:08:34,247 --> 00:08:35,942
Wagon tracks.

98
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:40,379
They've gone to Locksley, all right?

99
00:08:40,453 --> 00:08:42,318
Come on, let's go.

100
00:09:11,183 --> 00:09:13,174
Let's see it, then, the magic metal.

101
00:09:26,832 --> 00:09:29,130
- This it?
- Indeed.

102
00:09:29,201 --> 00:09:32,068
- It's very thin.
- Thin?

103
00:09:32,138 --> 00:09:34,572
Yes. But that is its beauty.

104
00:09:35,141 --> 00:09:37,905
With this on, a soldier can dance in battle.

105
00:09:37,977 --> 00:09:40,707
- Yes. How does it work?
- That is my secret.

106
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:44,641
And I am the only man west of Jerusalem
who knows how to make it.

107
00:09:44,717 --> 00:09:46,514
Ooh, la-di-da-di-da.

108
00:09:49,722 --> 00:09:51,314
O ye of little faith.

109
00:09:51,390 --> 00:09:54,359
Come. I will show you a little of my art.

110
00:09:58,664 --> 00:10:03,363
- Stinks like a Turk's trousers.
- To the artist, it is a beautiful smell.

111
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,131
Here, my special ingredient.

112
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,906
This to me is more precious than diamonds.

113
00:10:09,976 --> 00:10:13,139
I hope so. It's more expensive
than diamonds.

114
00:10:13,212 --> 00:10:15,009
Watch.

115
00:10:26,058 --> 00:10:27,992
Don't cough.

116
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:31,154
Breathe, inhale, enjoy.

117
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:32,822
Enjoy?

118
00:10:39,205 --> 00:10:40,797
Water for the Sheriff.

119
00:10:40,873 --> 00:10:43,933
Believe me, in time,
you will grow used to it.

120
00:10:45,511 --> 00:10:47,672
You will get used to it, my friend.

121
00:10:47,747 --> 00:10:51,114
Start production. I want
5,000 suits of armor.

122
00:10:51,751 --> 00:10:56,279
- My lord, that is a very great undertaking.
- Yes, your fee is very generous.

123
00:10:56,355 --> 00:10:58,880
The King of France would pay double.

124
00:11:05,031 --> 00:11:07,727
Well, you are indeed an artist.

125
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:13,935
- Double?
- An inconvenience.

126
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:17,237
But think of the gain.
An army of indestructible warriors.

127
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:21,172
Put this safely in my room.

128
00:11:27,253 --> 00:11:33,089
Gisborne... have you started a family
without telling me?

129
00:11:33,159 --> 00:11:34,751
My lord...

130
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:45,798
- Children.
- I caught them snooping around in the woods.

131
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:49,637
Tell me they didn't see you
testing the armor in the forest.

132
00:11:54,346 --> 00:11:59,045
- Why didn't you kill them, Gisborne?
- I decided we can use them in the mines.

133
00:11:59,118 --> 00:12:02,679
Just when I thought I could let you out
by yourself to flap your little wings,

134
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:05,349
you go and show compassion.

135
00:12:06,926 --> 00:12:11,363
When there are people who know
our little secret, those people have to die.

136
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:47,358
- That's the back-door plan.
- Come on, we move.

137
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,957
Every time.

138
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:22,600
Wait.

139
00:13:31,377 --> 00:13:33,777
I don't like waiting.

140
00:13:35,247 --> 00:13:38,080
Especially behind a cow.

141
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:41,517
- It's not good for my constitution.
- Much, shh!

142
00:14:17,623 --> 00:14:20,114
- Hood?
- It's Locksley to you.

143
00:14:25,231 --> 00:14:26,698
No.

144
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:30,199
Locksley's mine, now.

145
00:14:31,136 --> 00:14:33,696
Locksley will never be yours!

146
00:14:42,014 --> 00:14:42,981
Aaah!

147
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:50,948
Still sore? Face facts, Hood.

148
00:14:51,023 --> 00:14:53,082
You lost, I won.

149
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:06,534
Will, I need Allan and Djaq, now.

150
00:15:13,512 --> 00:15:15,605
You will not survive.

151
00:15:16,448 --> 00:15:20,384
It'll never happen,
no matter how many people you kill,

152
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:23,284
no matter how many children you terrify,

153
00:15:23,355 --> 00:15:25,983
no matter how much armor you put on.

154
00:15:30,629 --> 00:15:32,153
Ha!

155
00:15:32,231 --> 00:15:34,358
You overestimate me, Hood.

156
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:37,891
Sometimes at night,
I get one of your servants to rub my feet.

157
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:40,302
I don't care if she has heart or a mind.

158
00:15:40,372 --> 00:15:43,432
Step over there, cover your eyes,
I'll be back.

159
00:15:45,477 --> 00:15:47,035
OK?

160
00:15:47,146 --> 00:15:48,670
Aah!

161
00:15:56,021 --> 00:16:00,151
Ah! Rescued by outlaws. Quelle surprise.

162
00:16:00,225 --> 00:16:03,490
We fight. Take this. Defend me from above.

163
00:16:04,330 --> 00:16:06,230
Well, this should be fun.

164
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:10,761
- Come on!
- Where's Mark? You've left Mark.

165
00:16:10,836 --> 00:16:13,532
He's all right. We need you, now.

166
00:16:14,273 --> 00:16:16,298
You lot, stay here.

167
00:16:16,375 --> 00:16:18,434
In. Go in.

168
00:16:24,183 --> 00:16:28,176
- I can't let you keep these diamonds.
- And I can't let you take them.

169
00:16:28,253 --> 00:16:31,950
- The Black Knights would be disappointed.
- Then it's a stalemate.

170
00:16:33,258 --> 00:16:35,556
Shall we toss a coin for it?

171
00:16:35,627 --> 00:16:37,959
Not stalemate - checkmate.

172
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:41,962
Ahh!

173
00:16:42,034 --> 00:16:44,093
Ha ha! I'll see you.

174
00:16:52,644 --> 00:16:54,407
Ah! Son of a camel!

175
00:16:56,582 --> 00:16:58,482
Hood!

176
00:16:59,752 --> 00:17:01,151
Ah!

177
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:07,254
In the heat of battle, there is time
to watch your gang's back.

178
00:17:07,326 --> 00:17:09,089
Thanks, Daniel. Go, go!

179
00:17:33,552 --> 00:17:35,349
Aw!

180
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:37,218
This way!

181
00:17:39,525 --> 00:17:41,789
This is for the poor.

182
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:53,695
Gotcha!

183
00:18:07,719 --> 00:18:09,550
Come on, get in, get in.

184
00:18:13,225 --> 00:18:15,489
Is everyone all right?

185
00:18:15,561 --> 00:18:17,722
Wait. Where's Daniel?

186
00:18:18,697 --> 00:18:22,793
Gisborne! Robin Hood just knocked
one of my men out with a wooden box.

187
00:18:22,868 --> 00:18:26,360
Now you tell me it was not the box
with the black diamonds in it.

188
00:18:30,175 --> 00:18:34,544
- Five men and a boy!
- Hostage!

189
00:18:36,748 --> 00:18:39,080
Daniel.

190
00:18:39,151 --> 00:18:41,381
Robin Hood'll be back. He'll rescue me.

191
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:43,512
Counting on it.

192
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:47,423
People of Locksley. Let Robin Hood know this.

193
00:18:47,526 --> 00:18:51,326
We want our box and its contents
back by morning

194
00:18:51,864 --> 00:18:54,424
or his little friend will be punished.

195
00:18:55,868 --> 00:18:58,496
His little friend will die.

196
00:19:04,076 --> 00:19:07,102
Robin, we get the boy now.

197
00:19:07,179 --> 00:19:09,511
No, we stop and we think, John.

198
00:19:10,048 --> 00:19:12,312
You've gotta give him what he wants.

199
00:19:14,653 --> 00:19:17,520
Robin, take a look at this metal.

200
00:19:18,257 --> 00:19:20,691
It is Damascus steel or something like it.

201
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:23,726
A man wearing this will be invincible.

202
00:19:23,795 --> 00:19:27,390
- Western weapons would be useless.
- We can't let them make this stuff.

203
00:19:27,466 --> 00:19:31,698
- That's why I took the stones.
- We cannot give them back, Robin.

204
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:33,635
I know.

205
00:19:34,373 --> 00:19:36,841
- But we can't let the boy die.
- What do we do?

206
00:19:48,921 --> 00:19:50,513
Thank you.

207
00:20:17,783 --> 00:20:20,115
My guard's gone for a break.
We have two minutes.

208
00:20:20,185 --> 00:20:22,779
I heard about the boy. What do you want?

209
00:20:22,854 --> 00:20:26,915
The Sheriff's developing a new armor.
It'll make the Black Knights invincible.

210
00:20:26,992 --> 00:20:29,017
- We have to stop them.
- We can't risk the boy.

211
00:20:29,127 --> 00:20:30,617
I know.

212
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:34,130
But if the Sheriff defeats the King,
how many more lives will be lost?

213
00:20:34,199 --> 00:20:38,295
- My guard. I will get the boy out tonight.
- How? You're under house arrest?

214
00:20:38,370 --> 00:20:41,396
I will find a way.
That's the point of me being here.

215
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:49,771
Here, take this.

216
00:20:49,848 --> 00:20:53,511
- If Marian succeeds, we don't have to do this.
- But if she doesn't, we need a plan.

217
00:20:54,152 --> 00:20:55,813
Right...

218
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:59,982
We need to trade Daniel and the black
diamonds in open space, and that's here,

219
00:21:00,058 --> 00:21:03,789
so when the Sheriff has the diamonds
and we have Daniel back safely,

220
00:21:03,862 --> 00:21:05,386
then we can strike.

221
00:21:05,464 --> 00:21:09,366
You can't just nick them back, though.
Well, he'll have the place surrounded.

222
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:12,130
Might as well walk in saying, "Shoot me. "

223
00:21:12,204 --> 00:21:14,729
- We could destroy them.
- We'll have to.

224
00:21:14,806 --> 00:21:17,604
- We need something that burns quickly.
- Pitch.

225
00:21:17,676 --> 00:21:20,201
- Straw.
- It's fast but not hot enough.

226
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:22,304
- Pitch.
- Wood?

227
00:21:22,381 --> 00:21:25,680
- Wood's hot but it's not quick enough.
- Pitch.

228
00:21:25,751 --> 00:21:28,185
Fast burning and hot.

229
00:21:29,855 --> 00:21:32,983
Pitch! Good thinking, Mark.

230
00:21:33,058 --> 00:21:37,757
I could make a new box, choose the right
wood, something thin, could line it with pitch.

231
00:21:37,829 --> 00:21:41,526
Carry the black diamonds in that
then shoot it with a flaming arrow.

232
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:44,034
And the rocks will explode.

233
00:21:44,102 --> 00:21:46,662
Good idea, Will.
We'll test it in the morning.

234
00:21:46,738 --> 00:21:48,569
- Much?
- Hm?

235
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,609
Is this rat?

236
00:21:52,744 --> 00:21:55,611
- It's chicken.
- I can't see any feathers.

237
00:21:55,681 --> 00:21:58,673
No, and we haven't seen any squirrels.

238
00:22:00,052 --> 00:22:03,351
Right. I don't suppose any of you has noticed

239
00:22:03,422 --> 00:22:07,722
but I have to do everything you all
have to do and keep this larder stocked,

240
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:10,785
so if anyone else would care
to run themselves ragged in the forest,

241
00:22:10,862 --> 00:22:14,457
trying to catch some massive animal,
then you can be the servant!

242
00:22:39,057 --> 00:22:40,684
My lord.

243
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:46,588
My lord, I beg a favor of you.

244
00:22:47,399 --> 00:22:49,799
I have prepared a pass for you to sign.

245
00:22:49,868 --> 00:22:52,268
I need your permission to leave the castle.

246
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:57,267
- Why?
- You so decreed it.

247
00:22:57,342 --> 00:22:59,708
No, no, no.

248
00:22:59,778 --> 00:23:02,713
I mean, why do you need to leave?

249
00:23:04,616 --> 00:23:06,846
To visit Guy.

250
00:23:06,918 --> 00:23:08,681
Gisborne?

251
00:23:09,421 --> 00:23:10,911
Ooh.

252
00:23:10,989 --> 00:23:15,551
Well, he's had a bad day,
I don't advise it, hm?

253
00:23:15,627 --> 00:23:21,031
He should've killed some little boys
but he didn't, he let them live.

254
00:23:21,099 --> 00:23:22,964
Showed compassion.

255
00:23:23,769 --> 00:23:25,896
Now it's a mess.

256
00:23:32,544 --> 00:23:33,909
Hm.

257
00:23:33,979 --> 00:23:38,382
Well, then, perhaps now is a good time
for me to offer him an apology.

258
00:23:43,021 --> 00:23:44,989
At this hour?

259
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:50,960
And in your finest silks.

260
00:23:54,199 --> 00:23:55,894
I hope to make my peace with him.

261
00:24:05,544 --> 00:24:06,875
Please.

262
00:24:10,515 --> 00:24:13,075
Well... let me see.

263
00:24:18,056 --> 00:24:20,251
If it were me...

264
00:24:23,595 --> 00:24:26,587
I would slap your fickle face.

265
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:37,165
Both of them.

266
00:24:47,586 --> 00:24:49,816
This is a pass for the castle gate

267
00:24:49,888 --> 00:24:52,880
but underneath is an order
to send Daniel back to the castle

268
00:24:52,958 --> 00:24:54,949
so the Sheriff can question him tonight.

269
00:24:55,026 --> 00:24:59,861
Gisborne won't release him to us
but he will release him to a castle guard.

270
00:25:03,935 --> 00:25:05,994
I'll do it.

271
00:25:09,374 --> 00:25:11,308
Are you aware of the risk?

272
00:25:11,376 --> 00:25:14,607
- If Guy catches you...
- Don't worry. He'll be putty in my hands.

273
00:25:16,147 --> 00:25:18,672
- You're a brave man.
- Well...

274
00:25:22,787 --> 00:25:27,747
I'll go ahead. I told the Sheriff I'd call
on Gisborne, so I must show my face there.

275
00:25:27,826 --> 00:25:29,851
Good luck.

276
00:25:51,583 --> 00:25:53,312
Forgive me.

277
00:25:53,385 --> 00:25:55,216
Marian, it's late.

278
00:25:55,287 --> 00:25:57,414
Why so urgent?

279
00:25:57,489 --> 00:26:01,084
I wish to speak to you
about a personal matter.

280
00:26:04,362 --> 00:26:06,387
I'll send for you.

281
00:26:15,941 --> 00:26:18,000
Yeah? What is it?

282
00:26:18,109 --> 00:26:20,737
There is bad blood between us.

283
00:26:22,180 --> 00:26:24,478
You overestimate yourself.

284
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:29,577
I had feelings for you,
I made no bones about that.

285
00:26:30,689 --> 00:26:32,589
But now...

286
00:26:34,025 --> 00:26:36,357
I feel nothing.

287
00:26:38,096 --> 00:26:41,998
And I have larger concerns, ambitions.

288
00:26:42,968 --> 00:26:45,903
Is there no hope of a reconciliation?

289
00:26:45,971 --> 00:26:48,940
I know you are a man capable of compassion.

290
00:26:50,942 --> 00:26:52,910
I offer...

291
00:26:57,048 --> 00:26:58,709
I offer friendship.

292
00:27:05,824 --> 00:27:07,553
Guy...

293
00:27:13,331 --> 00:27:15,799
- What?
- I don't know.

294
00:27:15,867 --> 00:27:20,065
- Marian, what is this all about?
- It's about friendship, that's all.

295
00:27:20,138 --> 00:27:21,901
No.

296
00:27:23,775 --> 00:27:26,369
This isn't about friendship.

297
00:27:26,444 --> 00:27:30,972
You want your freedom back,
that's what this is all about

298
00:27:31,049 --> 00:27:33,609
and I can't give that to you.

299
00:27:34,619 --> 00:27:38,453
You and your father have made your own bed.

300
00:27:40,225 --> 00:27:43,319
Sorry, master.
There's a messenger from the Sheriff.

301
00:27:43,395 --> 00:27:45,659
I should go.

302
00:27:54,906 --> 00:27:57,739
- That looked friendly.
- You were spying on me?

303
00:27:57,809 --> 00:28:00,243
I was not spying. I was making sure
you were safe.

304
00:28:00,311 --> 00:28:03,906
I was safe. Shouldn't you
be making sure Allan is safe?

305
00:28:05,717 --> 00:28:07,742
I've played my part.

306
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:11,186
Marian.

307
00:28:14,959 --> 00:28:19,760
This is the Sheriff's official seal.
Who gave you this?

308
00:28:19,831 --> 00:28:24,598
Listen, mate, the fact you're standing there
holding that means I've stopped Robin, right?

309
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:28,369
I don't know where it's from.

310
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:32,467
You know, I start asking too many questions,
they're gonna blow my cover.

311
00:28:33,445 --> 00:28:36,209
- You did well to bring this to me.
- Yeah.

312
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:41,550
I know. I think I'll have a bit more wine.

313
00:28:48,827 --> 00:28:51,955
So... your plan's failed.

314
00:28:53,832 --> 00:28:56,198
What will Robin do?

315
00:28:56,301 --> 00:28:59,668
Well, if this doesn't work,
it's a straightforward swap.

316
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,899
Diamonds for boy.

317
00:29:01,973 --> 00:29:04,601
Robin wouldn't risk the boy's life,
not for anything.

318
00:29:05,376 --> 00:29:07,367
How very noble of him.

319
00:29:08,379 --> 00:29:10,472
But there must be some trick.

320
00:29:13,785 --> 00:29:15,719
What's it worth?

321
00:29:24,329 --> 00:29:26,354
Pitch.

322
00:29:26,431 --> 00:29:28,865
In a box containing the diamonds.

323
00:29:29,834 --> 00:29:33,167
Boy runs free,
Robin fires a flaming arrow and...

324
00:29:33,238 --> 00:29:35,798
"Pi-shoo!" Bye-bye, diamonds.

325
00:29:41,012 --> 00:29:44,607
- What will you tell Hood?
- Oh, that's easy.

326
00:29:44,716 --> 00:29:46,741
Just say I was tumbled.

327
00:29:46,818 --> 00:29:49,184
You recognized me, we had a fight,

328
00:29:49,254 --> 00:29:52,052
which, obviously, I nearly won,

329
00:29:52,624 --> 00:29:56,390
I left you for near-dead, fleeing the manor,
dispatching guards as I go.

330
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:59,456
Good idea.

331
00:30:02,767 --> 00:30:05,600
- What was that for?
- Believability.

332
00:30:09,541 --> 00:30:11,475
Allan.

333
00:30:11,543 --> 00:30:13,477
Shh.

334
00:30:13,545 --> 00:30:16,537
- Quick, let's go. Gisborne rumbled me.
- How did you get out?

335
00:30:16,614 --> 00:30:20,141
We had a scrap. I knocked him out.
Unbelievable.

336
00:30:20,218 --> 00:30:24,780
Luckily, his guards didn't hear us
but we should scarper before he comes to.

337
00:30:24,889 --> 00:30:27,858
- Right, come on.
- Robin.

338
00:30:27,926 --> 00:30:30,759
- I'm sorry.
- Eh, it's not your fault, is it?

339
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:34,458
We'll tell the others and Marian
it's Mark's pitch plan. Come on.

340
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:08,325
Right.

341
00:31:08,933 --> 00:31:10,798
Let's go.

342
00:31:10,902 --> 00:31:15,498
Guards, take him.
You, over there. Move it, move it.

343
00:31:19,210 --> 00:31:20,973
Here, boy.

344
00:31:21,045 --> 00:31:23,104
See that?

345
00:31:23,181 --> 00:31:27,174
If Robin Hood doesn't show up,
these people here will watch you swing.

346
00:31:27,252 --> 00:31:29,743
Sit.

347
00:31:32,123 --> 00:31:35,889
Well, I can see the sun.
No sign of your savior.

348
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:39,259
- He'll come.
- Mm? Oh, well, let's hope so, hmm?

349
00:31:39,330 --> 00:31:41,798
For your sake.

350
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:43,492
Hood!

351
00:31:46,371 --> 00:31:49,067
Oh, Robin Hood!

352
00:31:58,316 --> 00:32:00,807
Stay where you are, Hood.

353
00:32:03,021 --> 00:32:05,148
My smith will meet you in the middle,

354
00:32:05,223 --> 00:32:07,282
check the merchandise,

355
00:32:07,358 --> 00:32:10,350
if it's all right, you get the key
to the boy.

356
00:32:10,428 --> 00:32:13,226
No, Sheriff. You can make the exchange.

357
00:32:13,298 --> 00:32:16,392
Otherwise, your archers there will kill me.

358
00:32:16,501 --> 00:32:19,902
And if they do fire upon me,
my men will kill you.

359
00:32:21,039 --> 00:32:23,769
- Out of the way! Clear!
- Move! Move!

360
00:32:26,144 --> 00:32:27,736
Oh, la-di-da-di-da.

361
00:32:30,048 --> 00:32:32,175
Right, let's get on with it.

362
00:32:34,352 --> 00:32:38,982
Allan, Djaq, take the archers on the left.
You two, with me.

363
00:32:47,899 --> 00:32:52,097
Stop! You cannot release the child
to an outlaw.

364
00:32:52,770 --> 00:32:55,637
Somebody find me a box
and put this woman inside it.

365
00:32:55,707 --> 00:32:58,471
Release him to me.
I'll see that he gets home safely.

366
00:32:59,110 --> 00:33:02,409
Locksley, this makes no difference
to you, you have my word.

367
00:33:03,514 --> 00:33:05,914
- I accept these terms.
- Good for you.

368
00:33:08,519 --> 00:33:13,923
Go on, then. Now, the black diamonds.

369
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:15,857
Not yet.

370
00:33:15,927 --> 00:33:18,259
Allow me to check the merchandise first.

371
00:33:33,177 --> 00:33:35,111
Oh, so sorry.

372
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:39,616
You are, after all, as
Lady Marian pointed out...

373
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:44,879
...a murderous outlaw, hmm?

374
00:33:45,790 --> 00:33:47,849
The Sheriff's guessed our plan.

375
00:33:47,925 --> 00:33:49,586
Unbelievable.

376
00:33:49,694 --> 00:33:51,491
Something wrong, Hood?

377
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:01,938
Gisborne, all yours.

378
00:34:12,450 --> 00:34:14,748
That's the armor.

379
00:34:21,225 --> 00:34:24,092
Enjoy.

380
00:34:24,162 --> 00:34:25,891
Robin!

381
00:34:27,732 --> 00:34:29,791
Stay back! My sword!

382
00:34:29,867 --> 00:34:31,994
Master!

383
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:33,765
Yaah!

384
00:35:08,206 --> 00:35:10,197
Oh, fantastic!

385
00:35:13,344 --> 00:35:15,904
- What now, Locksley?
- Run!

386
00:35:28,226 --> 00:35:30,194
Master!

387
00:35:30,294 --> 00:35:33,957
- Robin!
- Don't touch him! Stay on the archers!

388
00:35:38,903 --> 00:35:40,564
No, John, wait!

389
00:35:54,585 --> 00:35:56,576
Locksley will always be mine.

390
00:36:00,024 --> 00:36:02,049
What's he doing?

391
00:36:02,126 --> 00:36:04,526
Is that the best you can do?

392
00:36:05,163 --> 00:36:07,131
What now?

393
00:36:08,132 --> 00:36:10,123
Playing outlaws with the children?

394
00:36:11,135 --> 00:36:13,467
Goodbye, Hood.

395
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:16,166
- Oh, no.
- Oh, yes.

396
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:44,495
Tell your men to withdraw, Sheriff!

397
00:36:45,836 --> 00:36:48,066
Another exchange -

398
00:36:48,139 --> 00:36:50,334
the black diamonds for Gisborne

399
00:36:50,408 --> 00:36:52,433
and you have him back!

400
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:55,138
Well, how long can you hold your breath?

401
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:57,010
My lord, please!

402
00:36:57,114 --> 00:37:01,073
You, er, you seem to have overestimated
Gisborne's importance to me.

403
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:04,711
Make sure he's safe.

404
00:37:05,790 --> 00:37:07,417
Urghh!

405
00:37:07,525 --> 00:37:09,857
Not even you would let him die.

406
00:37:09,927 --> 00:37:12,953
Erm, I have everything I could want.

407
00:37:13,030 --> 00:37:15,396
- Sheriff!
- Oh, no, not again.

408
00:37:17,535 --> 00:37:19,366
- Let him live.
- Who?

409
00:37:19,437 --> 00:37:21,496
Guy.

410
00:37:22,974 --> 00:37:25,807
- Marian, what are you doing?
- I am asking you to reconsider.

411
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:27,969
You are helping Hood?

412
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:33,213
Quite the opposite. I am reminding you
that Sir Guy is your most loyal servant.

413
00:37:33,317 --> 00:37:34,716
Oh!

414
00:37:34,785 --> 00:37:37,481
- My lord! Please!
- Let him die.

415
00:37:37,555 --> 00:37:39,546
He's a noble and a good man.

416
00:37:39,624 --> 00:37:42,354
He must be worth more to you
than a sack of rocks.

417
00:37:42,426 --> 00:37:44,485
I will have those rocks.

418
00:37:45,830 --> 00:37:47,388
Then I will kill this man.

419
00:37:48,299 --> 00:37:51,735
Without him, are the rocks really any use?

420
00:37:51,802 --> 00:37:53,702
Er, no, no, they are not.

421
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:57,263
I am the only man west of Jerusalem
who can make them work their magic.

422
00:38:03,381 --> 00:38:05,110
- My lord!
- Shut up!

423
00:38:10,354 --> 00:38:12,720
My lord, I will get you more rocks.

424
00:38:20,331 --> 00:38:22,629
You will be punished for this, Marian.

425
00:38:22,700 --> 00:38:25,430
Be in no doubt - you'll be punished.

426
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:46,187
Burn these.

427
00:39:15,653 --> 00:39:17,985
You saved my life. I'm grateful.

428
00:39:19,557 --> 00:39:21,548
Well, I could not watch
you die and do nothing.

429
00:39:22,660 --> 00:39:26,528
- You saved Robin, too.
- That was incidental.

430
00:39:26,597 --> 00:39:28,462
Was it?

431
00:39:30,334 --> 00:39:33,929
Marian, I've been assuming
that since Hood became an outlaw

432
00:39:34,004 --> 00:39:36,700
that you've had nothing further
to do with him. Was I wrong?

433
00:39:36,774 --> 00:39:38,833
- No.
- Because if you were

434
00:39:38,909 --> 00:39:41,935
associating with an outlaw,

435
00:39:42,012 --> 00:39:44,139
the punishment wouldn't be house arrest,

436
00:39:44,215 --> 00:39:47,082
the punishment would be death.

437
00:39:47,151 --> 00:39:49,176
Would you prefer me to have let you die?

438
00:39:52,623 --> 00:39:55,888
Gisborne. Stay there!

439
00:39:56,827 --> 00:39:59,728
Wait, wait, wait. Where are you going?

440
00:39:59,797 --> 00:40:03,130
- I cannot work in this environment.
- My dear friend,

441
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:05,691
we could agree to increase your fee?

442
00:40:05,770 --> 00:40:08,762
In France, they know how to treat an artist.

443
00:40:17,381 --> 00:40:20,077
- What were you thinking?
- Guy is your faithful servant.

444
00:40:20,151 --> 00:40:24,019
- I was preventing your mistake.
- You do not prevent my mistakes!

445
00:40:24,088 --> 00:40:26,556
You must be punished.

446
00:40:26,624 --> 00:40:28,956
I am ready for your punishment.

447
00:40:31,595 --> 00:40:33,529
Yes.

448
00:40:33,597 --> 00:40:36,395
- But is your father?
- You leave him out of this.

449
00:40:36,467 --> 00:40:42,463
Oh, I will leave him, all right. Alone, to rot
in a dungeon, until you learn to behave yourself.

450
00:40:45,309 --> 00:40:46,970
No.

451
00:40:57,855 --> 00:41:00,119
- A toast.
- Just hang on.

452
00:41:01,158 --> 00:41:03,023
Djaq, Will...

453
00:41:07,898 --> 00:41:10,093
Good work, lads.

454
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:17,400
You are now
honorary members of our gang.

455
00:41:18,108 --> 00:41:21,305
You are eyes and ears in the villages.

456
00:41:21,378 --> 00:41:23,312
And any time you need us...

457
00:41:25,216 --> 00:41:26,979
you can call on us.

458
00:41:27,051 --> 00:41:29,884
Any time you need us, call on us.

459
00:41:29,954 --> 00:41:31,819
That's a deal.

460
00:41:31,889 --> 00:41:34,551
We are Robin Hood!

461
00:41:34,992 --> 00:41:37,392
We are Robin Hood.

